  "term": "gray matter",
  "definition": "Gray matter is the darker-looking tissue in the central nervous system compared with white matter. It is made up mainly of neuron cell bodies, surrounding nerve tissue, glial cells, and capillaries, with relatively few myelinated nerve fibers.",
